 "utterances": [
  {
   "start": 5.94,
   "end": 9.09,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Morning, everyone. Monday the thirteenth. You all hearing me?"
  },
  {
   "start": 9.96,
   "end": 12.76,
   "speaker_id": "p02",
   "speaker": "David Whitfield",
   "text": "Yep. Bit tinny, but that's probably this headset."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.2,
   "end": 16.95,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "You're coming through fine here."
  },
  {
   "start": 17.58,
   "end": 20.03,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Right, lovely. Everyone survived the weekend, then?"
  },
  {
   "start": 20.79,
   "end": 24.99,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "More importantly, there's a birthday cake in the office. Proper big one."
  },
  {
   "start": 26.49,
   "end": 27.69,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Whose birthday?"
  },
  {
   "start": 29.94,
   "end": 34.49,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Didn't get that far. Saw the cake, thought you'd want the important information."
  },
  {
   "start": 35.74,
   "end": 36.94,
   "speaker_id": "p11",
   "speaker": "Hannah Price",
   "text": "Excellent investigation, that."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.32,
   "end": 41.12,
   "speaker_id": "p03",
   "speaker": "Priya Raman",
   "text": "Has it actually got a name on it?"
  },
  {
   "start": 42.25,
   "end": 44.35,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Probably under the bit that's missing."
  },
  {
   "start": 45.21,
   "end": 50.46,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Right, before this becomes cake forensics, Jamie Brennan's absent today. We've got everyone else on."
  },
  {
   "start": 51.98,
   "end": 54.08,
   "speaker_id": "p11",
   "speaker": "Hannah Price",
   "text": "Yeah. Shall I start with mine?"
  },
  {
   "start": 56.3,
   "end": 63.3,
   "speaker_id": "p11",
   "speaker": "Hannah Price",
   "text": "The near-miss write-up — I've had a first look, nothing major so far. Only at the initial notes stage, though."
  },
  {
   "start": 65.75,
   "end": 66.95,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Okay, cheers."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.35,
   "end": 74.35,
   "speaker_id": "p02",
   "speaker": "David Whitfield",
   "text": "Hannah asked me to pass on the pressure-drop investigation. That's cancelled our end; the supplier's doing it under warranty instead."
  },
  {
   "start": 76.34,
   "end": 77.74,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Fair enough, makes sense."
  },
  {
   "start": 79.47,
   "end": 86.82,
   "speaker_id": "p11",
   "speaker": "Hannah Price",
   "text": "And recalibrating the sensors on the heater box on one has moved to next week. That's the new deadline for mine."
  },
  {
   "start": 87.85,
   "end": 89.05,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Yep, understood."
  },
  {
   "start": 89.51,
   "end": 100.01,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Pricey asked me to mention the filter swap on CT1 as well. She's had a first look, nothing major so far, but hasn't got as far as the swap yet."
  },
  {
   "start": 100.42,
   "end": 101.62,
   "speaker_id": "p02",
   "speaker": "David Whitfield",
   "text": "Mm, okay."
  },
  {
   "start": 103.78,
   "end": 109.03,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "And I already swapped the filter on the chiller on three yesterday. That one's sorted."
  },
  {
   "start": 110.31,
   "end": 114.16,
   "speaker_id": "p02",
   "speaker": "David Whitfield",
   "text": "Ah, good. Lovely when they actually come out without a fight."
  },
  {
   "start": 116.07,
   "end": 122.02,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "On my training records for the new starters, I've done the prep. Just the write-up left now."
  },
  {
   "start": 122.81,
   "end": 125.61,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Thanks. Um, one handover from me as well."
  },
  {
   "start": 126.54,
   "end": 133.89,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Organising the toolbox talk for the team — I'm handing that over to Olumide Adeyemi. Can you take that from me?"
  },
  {
   "start": 134.4,
   "end": 137.2,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Yeah, I'll take over organising the toolbox talk."
  },
  {
   "start": 138.69,
   "end": 141.84,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Cheers. Right, today's new bits. What's happening on two?"
  },
  {
   "start": 143.7,
   "end": 148.25,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "The line 2 robot's jammed. Production's held up on that at the minute."
  },
  {
   "start": 148.67,
   "end": 152.87,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Is it just the jam, or are the sensors involved as well?"
  },
  {
   "start": 154.99,
   "end": 161.99,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Can't call the sensors good yet. It needs clearing and those checking, not just pulling the jam out and assuming."
  },
  {
   "start": 163.16,
   "end": 166.31,
   "speaker_id": "p02",
   "speaker": "David Whitfield",
   "text": "Yeah, a clear gap isn't necessarily a happy sensor."
  },
  {
   "start": 167.78,
   "end": 176.53,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the line 2 robot by tomorrow morning. That's holding production up so it needs doing first."
  },
  {
   "start": 177.71,
   "end": 179.46,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Thanks, Saz. That's yours, then."
  },
  {
   "start": 180.19,
   "end": 181.59,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Yep, I'll take it."
  },
  {
   "start": 182.11,
   "end": 188.06,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Mide, can you take vibration readings on the hot bearing by Monday? Drop everything for that one."
  },
  {
   "start": 188.58,
   "end": 192.08,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Yeah, I'll take the vibration readings on the hot bearing."
  },
  {
   "start": 192.98,
   "end": 197.88,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Monday as in today, yeah? Just checking, not trying to buy myself a week."
  },
  {
   "start": 198.34,
   "end": 200.44,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Today, yes. Definitely not next Monday."
  },
  {
   "start": 202.32,
   "end": 203.72,
   "speaker_id": "p02",
   "speaker": "David Whitfield",
   "text": "Worth a try, though."
  },
  {
   "start": 205.69,
   "end": 209.19,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Ha. No, understood — that one takes priority for me."
  },
  {
   "start": 209.77,
   "end": 213.27,
   "speaker_id": "p03",
   "speaker": "Priya Raman",
   "text": "And I'll run the monthly fire alarm test on Friday."
  },
  {
   "start": 214.1,
   "end": 215.3,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Thanks, Pri. Agreed."
  },
  {
   "start": 217.16,
   "end": 220.66,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Friday's getting a theme. Isn't that cake day as well?"
  },
  {
   "start": 221.51,
   "end": 226.41,
   "speaker_id": "p03",
   "speaker": "Priya Raman",
   "text": "The charity bake sale on Friday, yeah. Nothing engineering-related about that, before anyone starts."
  },
  {
   "start": 227.19,
   "end": 229.29,
   "speaker_id": "p11",
   "speaker": "Hannah Price",
   "text": "Depends how your sponge turns out."
  },
  {
   "start": 229.95,
   "end": 231.35,
   "speaker_id": "p03",
   "speaker": "Priya Raman",
   "text": "Oi. Structurally sound, mine."
  },
  {
   "start": 233.14,
   "end": 235.94,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "All right, any other observations before we finish?"
  },
  {
   "start": 237.58,
   "end": 243.53,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Only that I heard a slight rattle from the Atlas. Nothing to action yet, just an observation."
  },
  {
   "start": 245.81,
   "end": 247.91,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Okay, noted. No action off that."
  },
  {
   "start": 249.3,
   "end": 253.5,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Sorry, did I clip out halfway through? Teams went a bit funny."
  },
  {
   "start": 254.17,
   "end": 257.67,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "No, we got you. Your picture froze, voice was fine."
  },
  {
   "start": 259.51,
   "end": 261.61,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Probably an improvement, the frozen picture."
  },
  {
   "start": 263.08,
   "end": 264.48,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Wouldn't like to comment."
  },
  {
   "start": 265.18,
   "end": 267.63,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Very diplomatic. Right, that's us. Thanks, everyone."
  },
  {
   "start": 269.31,
   "end": 270.51,
   "speaker_id": "p03",
   "speaker": "Priya Raman",
   "text": "Cheers, all."
  },
  {
   "start": 271.16,
   "end": 272.36,
   "speaker_id": "p02",
   "speaker": "David Whitfield",
   "text": "Cheers."
  }
 ],
